.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt ARC4RANDOM 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm arc4random
.Nm arc4random_buf
.Nm arc4random_uniform
.Nm getentropy
.Nm getrandom
.Nd random data
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In stdlib.h
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn arc4random void
.Ft void
.Fn arc4random_buf "void *buffer" "size_t length"
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn arc4random_uniform "uint32_t bound"
.Ft int
.Fn getentropy "void *buffer" "size_t length"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn getrandom "void *buffer" "size_t length" "unsigned int flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions return random bytes from the system random source. The arc4random family
never fails; getentropy and getrandom report errors.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn arc4random returns a 32-bit value. .Fn arc4random_uniform returns a value below the bound.
.Fn getentropy returns 0. .Fn getrandom returns the byte count.
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn getentropy fails with .Er EIO when the source is unavailable. .Fn getrandom returns -1
with .Er EAGAIN or .Er EINVAL.
.Sh STANDARDS
BSD and Linux interfaces; ring 1 and ring 2.
.Sh CAVEATS
The functions are seeded from the rand: scheme or GETRANDOM. The ENTROPY_WEAK interim is a
release blocker, not a libc-gate blocker; see H-5 and C50.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getrandom 3
.Xr libc 7
